d at standard' is incorrect. Add a note at line 198: '(see ## Reflect Depth (Deterministic TCS) O4 override for skill-only mode)' and ensure the section distinguishes the two.\",\n      \"cross_references\": [],\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"CLI mode executor_model_class comment uses 'removal directive' language contradicting instance-level independence\",\n      \"category\": \"consistency\",\n      \"severity_hint\": \"low\",\n      \"file\": \"src/superclaude/skills/task-builder/SKILL.md\",\n      \"line\": 159,\n      \"line_range_end\": 159,\n      \"in_diff\": true,\n      \"evidence\": \"\\\"executor_model_class: \\\"<executor model-class alias, e.g. sonnet: recorded PROVENANCE of which class executed; passed through to reflect as a compat field. OUR sc-reflect does NOT class-exclude (instance-level independence); this class is NOT removed from the reviewer pool.>\\\"\\\"\",\n      \"why\": \"Line 159 (frontmatter comment for executor_model_class in CLI mode) correctly states 'this class is NOT removed from the reviewer pool', but the CLI POST note §4 clause 3 (lines 211-218) requires 'Comment hygiene. The executor_model_class frontmatter comment uses recorded-provenance / compat language only, never a removal-directive wording (it must not claim the named class is dropped from the reviewer panel).' The comment at line 159 includes both 'NOT removed' (correct) and 'recorded PROVENANCE... passed through to reflect as a compat field' (correct), so it passes hygiene. However, the comment should avoid the word 'exclude' entirely to prevent any inference of removal semantics.\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Minor wording tweak at line 159: change 'does NOT class-exclude' to 'does NOT remove the executor class from the reviewer pool'. This avoids the word 'exclude' which could be read as acknowledging the existence of an exclusion mechanism. Alternatively, use 'keeps the executor class in the reviewer pool' (positive framing).