el independence (no class removal, --executor-model accepted-and-ignored). If it does, cite the contract version explicitly: 'The skill (sc-reflect v1.5.1+) no longer excludes any model class; reviewer-panel independence is guaranteed at the instance level (fresh subagent + no formation context + blind calibration), not by class removal.' If v1.5.1 has not shipped, mark the claim as contingent: 'PENDING sc-reflect v1.5.1: instance-level independence (class stays in pool, independence via fresh spawn). Until v1.5.1 ships, the class-exclusion mechanism remains active and executor_model_class is used for removal.'\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Unvalidated default path shipping without user warning is a release-gate violation\",\n      \"category\": \"anti-pattern\",\n      \"severity_hint\": \"critical\",\n      \"affected_files\": [\"src/superclaude/skills/task-builder/SKILL.md\"],\n      \"why\": \"The author states 'ONLY the wrapper path is session-validated end-to-end; the skill-default path is NOT yet validated.' This means the default code path (skill-only POST, --cli absent) ships unvalidated. Shipping an unvalidated default violates the release-gate principle: the most-used path should be the most-tested path. Users invoking task-builder without --cli get an untested POST gate with no disclosure. The SKILL.md should either (a) mark skill-only mode as EXPERIMENTAL and recommend --cli, or (b) block the release until skill-only is validated. Shipping both paths with the untested one as default is a recipe for production failures.\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"CRITICAL ACTION: Either (1) invert the default (make --cli the default, skill-only the opt-in flag --experimental-skill-only), OR (2) add a loud WARNING at the top of the SKILL.md and in the #6 input description: 'WARNING: The skill-only POST gate (default) is NOT session-validated. Use --cli for production work until validation completes (issue #XXX).' OR (3) block the PR until skill-only validation is complete. The current state (untested default, no warning) is unacceptable for a production release.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notes_for_orchestrator\": \"Review focused on the RF SKILLS chunk (task-builder, task, tech-research, tech-reference) per the specified scope. Findings concentrate on the --cli toggle bifurcation and the instance-level independence anti-self-confirmation mechanism. The most critical issue is the unvalidated skill-only default path shipping without user disclosure (anti-pattern finding #3 + cross-cutting observation #3). The contract-version mismatch (finding #5) requires verification: if sc-reflect v1.5.1 has not merged, all instance-level independence claims are premature. The spec-path threading contradictions (findings #1, #4) are medium-severity correctness issues that create ambiguity about CLI vs skill-only behavior. All findings cite real file:line evidence from the diff or HEAD state.\"\n}\n```\n","is_error":false,"subtype":"success","session_id":"20ff72ed-354d-4926-b1cf-a6ea43201aa3","num_turns":0,"request_id":"0df6c3e1-4d06-4ceb-94ad-0e3f8af63f3a"}
